   $q$Sentence (2) is informal and unclear. Which revision states the claim most clearly and formally?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The depot is a very old building on Front Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-claim"},{"text":"Some people like the depot, and other people like parking lots.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-position"},{"text":"I kind of think the depot is pretty cool and should maybe stay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Millbrook should turn the old depot into a history museum instead of tearing it down.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Millbrook should turn the old depot into a history museum instead of tearing it down.$q$, $q$The correct revision takes a precise, formal position that the reasons in sentences (3) through (5) support. The first choice keeps the casual, uncertain wording of the original.$q$, 'draft', 'a403329d-ccee-58fc-b1b7-63d03a6a0a78')
