   $q$Which statement best explains how sentences (5) and (6) support the claim in sentence (3)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They show that Birchwood students waste food because lunch is too short.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They show that a real school that made the same change threw away less food, which suggests Birchwood could too.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They prove that every school in the country should move recess before lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"They present the opposing side's reason for keeping lunch before recess.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They show that a real school that made the same change threw away less food, which suggests Birchwood could too.$q$, $q$Sentences (5) and (6) report the results of the same change at another school, which supports trying it at Birchwood. One school's results cannot prove what every school in the country should do.$q$, 'draft', 'b2c37795-fa1a-563f-80bc-8cfe2231e247')
